WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
1 PDF template + 1 Excel sheet = all your documents filled in.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.100
Tap “Open a PDF”.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.500
Pick the document to fill in: here, a blank certificate.

4
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.700
Now it needs some data.

5
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.900
Tap “Open Excel/CSV”.

6
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.100
Pick your Excel or CSV file.

7
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:28.100
Your sheet has 3 rows: the app shows 1/3 and will create 3 certificates.

8
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:31.300
Tap the + button.

9
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.300
These are your sheet’s columns. Let’s start with the name.

10
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:39.100
Tap where the name should go.

11
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:43.500
It shows the column name. Each document gets the value from its row.

12
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.700
Date, subject, place…

13
00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:53.300
Drag a field to move it. Tap it to change its size or delete it.

14
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.500
Tap “Generate”.

15
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:01.100
Nothing is saved yet. Tap “Choose a folder”.

16
00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:06.100
Tap “Save”. Without it, your documents aren’t kept.

17
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.700
Your 3 PDFs are in a ZIP file, in the folder you chose.

18
00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:16.200
Here are your 3 certificates. One per row of the sheet.

19
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.800
Try a ready-made template from the home screen.

20
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:24.400
Free for up to 5 rows per run.
